# Post-merge: ledger tester + fix (required)

**On every merge** (and before calling a feature PR “done”), do both:

1. **Ledger / tester canary** — a test that fails if this class of bug returns
   (route regression, UI dual-view/tab test, step-verification ledger entry, or
   hygiene canary — whichever matches the surface).
2. **The fix in the same landing** — Greptile P2s, missing session gates, happy-path-only
   mint/resolve, and “no route/UI test” are not follow-ups to forget. Ship them in the
   feature PR or an immediate harden PR on the same day.

## Do not leave

- Merged feature with failed CI (~seconds, empty steps) marked done without a green
  follow-up once Actions can run, **and** without local canaries locked.
- New surfaces (`/summary-inflow`, Login/In-flow tabs, mint paths) with only happy-path
  coverage.

## Dual-view resource server example (#780 / #781)

Canaries (must stay tracked and green locally):

- `demo_api_server/src/__tests__/resourceServer.summaryInflow.regression.test.js`
- `demo_api_ui/src/components/__tests__/ResourceServerPage.dualView.test.jsx`
- `resolveTokenAsync` edge cases in `resourceServerTester.test.js`
- Hygiene locks in `scripts/check-fresh-clone-hygiene.js` (summary-inflow session gate,
  `startsWith('banking:')`, mint subject-AT check)

If any of those disappear or the source contracts regress, fix immediately — do not
open a new feature until the canary is green again.
